Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.37,0:00:06.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Now turn one {\c&H7AAF1B&}knob{\c&HF7F4F2&} on this flow: Rm.\NTurning it up means less diffusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.99,0:00:09.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Less smudging should\Nonly help the stretching.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.38,0:00:14.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}So once the dynamo switches\Non, it stays on. Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.16,0:00:21.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Here is the growth rate,\Ncomputed at twenty-four settings.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.77,0:00:27.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Below about nine, every {\c&H3468EB&}field{\c&HF7F4F2&} fades. Then\Ngrowth turns positive: the dynamo is on.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.00,0:00:31.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Near seventeen and a half,\Nit switches off again.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.32,0:00:34.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Above about twenty-seven, it comes back.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.06,0:00:40.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Not one threshold, but windows: turning\Na knob further does not always help.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.73,0:00:43.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}It agrees with published\Nresults. No machine
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.82,0:00:47.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}learning yet: this only tests the solver.
